          "event": "Flood Watch",
          "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
          "senderName": "NWS Miami FL",
          "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 1 at 12:49PM EST until November 2 at 3:00PM EST by NWS Miami FL",
          "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southeast Florida, including the following\nareas, Coastal Broward County, Coastal Miami Dade County, Coastal\nPalm Beach County, Far South Miami-Dade County, Inland Broward\nCounty, Inland Miami-Dade County, Inland Palm Beach County, Metro\nBroward County, Metro Palm Beach County and Metropolitan Miami\nDade.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Isolated to scattered area of flash flooding will be\npossible, with the main impact being street flooding, road\nclosures, and limited impact to structures in flood prone areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Uncertainty is high regarding exactly where the highest rain\namounts will fall. However, scattered locations across the east\ncoast may pick up 3 to 5 inches of rain through Monday. Isolated\nspots may see accumulations as high as 5 to 7 inches. These\namounts may fall over a window of a few hours. Expected impacts\ncould be greater than forecast if the heaviest rainfall occurs\nnear the coast during times of high tide.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
          "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
          "response": "Prepare",
          "note": null,
